Use Tailwind v4's `@custom-variant` directive in your CSS to register a `pwa:` variant tied to the media feature:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

@custom-variant pwa (@media all and (display-mode: standalone));
```

Then use it anywhere: `<button className="mb-2 md:mb-4 pwa:mb-6 ...">`. This works exactly like the `theme-midnight:` example (arbitrary variant → reusable named variant), so no `tailwind.config.js` needed.

**Source:** `src/docs/hover-focus-and-other-states.mdx`, "Registering a custom variant" section (~line 2974-2991).

